{"title":"Career Roadmap · Automobile Designer","role":"Automobile Designer","summary":"ID: 1659\nLevel: UG\nCategory: Media, Design & Creative Arts\nDegree: B.Des (Bachelor of Design)\nSpecialization: Transportation / Automobile Design\nCareer: Automobile Designer","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Automobile Designer designs the visual, functional and experiential aspects of vehicles such as cars, motorcycles, commercial vehicles, electric vehicles and mobility concepts."},{"type":"p","text":"The role combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Industrial design"},{"text":"Transportation design"},{"text":"Automotive engineering awareness"},{"text":"Sketching and visualisation"},{"text":"3D modelling"},{"text":"CAD"},{"text":"Ergonomics"},{"text":"Materials and manufacturing"},{"text":"User experience"},{"text":"Aerodynamics awareness"},{"text":"Sustainable mobility"},{"text":"Electric and autonomous vehicle design"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Automobile designers generally work in multidisciplinary teams with automotive engineers, UX designers, clay modellers, CMF designers, product planners and manufacturing teams."}]},{"heading":"Typical Education Route","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Transportation/Automobile Design","Automotive Design Internship","Portfolio/Showreel","Junior Automotive Designer","Transportation Designer","Senior Designer","Design Lead/Design Director"]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong undergraduate portfolio is often as important as the degree itself for design recruitment."}]},{"heading":"Career Development Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Horizon","Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Design fundamentals, drawing, observation, form"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Transportation design, digital modelling, CAD"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Automotive projects, clay/3D modelling, intern